    "created_by": "leonardmarcq",
    "output": "Absolutely! Diversifying your portfolio with sustainable investments is a great idea. Here are a few tips:\n\n1. **Research Sustainable Funds**: Look for mutual funds or ETFs that focus on ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance) criteria. Funds like these typically invest in companies that are committed to sustainable practices.\n\n2. **Consider Green Bonds**: These are fixed-income securities that fund projects with positive environmental impacts. They can be a stable investment while supporting sustainability.\n\n3. **Invest in Clean Technology**: Look into companies that are innovating in areas like renewable energy, energy efficiency, and electric vehicles. These sectors are seeing growth as the world shifts towards greener practices.\n\n4. **Check Company Ratings**: Platforms like MSCI or Sustainalytics provide ratings for companies based on their sustainability efforts. This can be helpful in identifying solid investment opportunities.\n\n5. **Support Local Enterprises**: Sometimes investing in local sustainable businesses or start-ups can yield good returns while also supporting your community.\n\nAlways make sure to do thorough research and consider consulting a financial advisor who specializes in sustainable investing. Good luck!",
